# CorsaIQ — Next.js App Router, Tailwind CSS, TypeScript

Keep this file as project-wide defaults. Prefer Server Components, typed APIs, and utility-first Tailwind.

## Next.js (App Router)

- Use the App Router under `src/app`. Folders define routes; `page.tsx` and `layout.tsx` define UI.
- Keep the root layout as the only place with `<html>` and `<body>`. Nested layouts wrap `children`.
- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only for state, effects, event handlers, or browser APIs.
- Colocate Client Components at the leaves. Fetch data and secrets in Server Components; pass serializable props down.
- Use `next/link` for internal navigation (prefetch). Use `<a>` only for external URLs.
- Use `next/image` for images (`alt`, explicit width/height or `fill`).
- Export `metadata` or `generateMetadata` from Server Components. Do not set document title in client effects.
- Await `params` and `searchParams` (they are Promises). Type route props; do not use `any`.
- Put Route Handlers in `route.ts`. Keep secrets on the server; never expose them to the client bundle.
- Prefer the `@/` alias from `tsconfig.json` (`@/*` → `src/*`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — client page for static marketing UI
"use client";
export default function Page() {
  return <h1>CorsaIQ</h1>;
}

// ✅ GOOD — Server Component + Link
import Link from "next/link";

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <main>
      <h1>CorsaIQ</h1>
      <Link href="#features">Bekijk features</Link>
    </main>
  );
}
```

## TypeScript

- Keep `strict` on. Prefer `unknown` + narrowing over `any`.
- Type public component props explicitly. Derive unions from `as const` data when possible.
- Handle errors with typed results or custom error classes; do not swallow exceptions.
- Prefer named exports for shared modules; default-export only `page`, `layout`, and `route` files.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
function score(value: any) {
  return value.points;
}

// ✅ GOOD
type Metric = { points: number };

function score(value: Metric): number {
  return value.points;
}
```

## Tailwind CSS (v4)

- Style with utilities. Put design tokens in `src/app/globals.css` (`@theme inline`), not scattered magic numbers.
- Use `globals.css` for resets and tokens only. Prefer utilities in components over new CSS files.
- Mobile-first: unprefixed classes, then `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`.
- Prefer semantic HTML + Tailwind over extra wrappers. Use `gap-*` instead of margin soup.
- Keep hover/focus styles and visible focus rings. Do not remove outlines without a replacement.
- Avoid `@apply` except for a tiny set of repeated primitives.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="box" style={{ marginTop: 32 }} />

// ✅ GOOD
<section className="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
  <article className="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 p-6" />
</section>
```

## Accessibility and quality

- One `h1` per page. Nest headings in order.
- Buttons and links need an accessible name. Icons-only controls need `aria-label`.
- Do not commit `.env` secrets. Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_` only for values that must run in the browser.
